    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d693">

                <pb facs="0881" n="791" sameAs="frus:frus1934v03/pg791"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.6363 Manchuria/112: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-12-15T12:00:00+09:00">December 15,
                        1934—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received December 15—5:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>276. The Netherlands Minister on December 13 made formal representations to the
                    Japanese Government on the subject of the oil monopoly in Manchuria, leaving
                    with the Foreign Office an <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> along
                    substantially the same lines as the British <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >aide-mémoire</hi> of November 24. Full text by mail.<anchor n="83"
                        xml:id="d693-f1"/></p>
                <p>Repeated by mail to Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
